In article <MEISSNER.94Jun5214725@pasta.osf.org> meissner@osf.org (Michael Meissner) writes:
>the big room, barracks, etc.).  Rather than having to hit space after each and
>every message, it would be useful if the game switched to the More interface
>when there is more than one line.  That way you can read twenty messages at
>once on a terminal, and have a scrolling winding under X to handle the
>messages.  The same goes when you are frozen by a floating eye, and get
>multiple hits from monsters.

Under the X11 interface, you can set the size of the message area. Though
there is a limit. But the message window does include a scroll bar for those
that go off the top. Also in this area (under X11) is a message line, for
separating old and new messages (old being the messages from the last turn
or before). The was a bug with this line pre 313, but is now fixed
(My first offical bug fix!:-)

Also, if using an Amiga (no flames please!), and if the screen is big
enough, you can also have a larger message window. Persumably, Macs do the
same thing (anyone comfirm/deny thigs?)

The one line only is only there for small(?) tty windows (standard size
being 24x80), and one line is all that will fit!

I haven't been using X11 for too long, so I can't rightly remember how to
set the size for X11. But it is there... Its in the source there
somewhere...

